MAXIMUM FREQUENCY STACK (FREQSTACK)
🟢 Problem Statement

Design a stack-like data structure that supports:

push(int val)

pop()

Rules:

pop() should remove and return the most frequent element.

If multiple elements have same highest frequency → remove the most recently added.

🔎 Example
Operations:
push(5)
push(7)
push(5)
push(7)
push(4)
push(5)

pop() → 5
pop() → 7
pop() → 5
pop() → 4

🧠 Why?

Frequency state:

Element	Frequency
5	3
7	2
4	1

First pop:

5 has highest freq (3)

Second pop:

5 → freq becomes 2

Now 5 & 7 both freq = 2

Most recent among them → 7

🟢 Why This Is Tricky?

You need:

Frequency tracking

Maintain order

Fast O(1) operations

Normal stack won't work.
PriorityQueue alone won't work.
We need combination of:

💡 HashMap + Stack + MaxFrequency tracker
🟢 Key Idea

We maintain:

1️⃣ freqMap
→ element → frequency

2️⃣ groupMap
→ frequency → stack of elements

3️⃣ maxFreq
→ current highest frequency

🟢 Structure Idea

If:

5 appears 3 times


We push it into:

groupMap[1]
groupMap[2]
groupMap[3]


So when popping:
We directly look at stack of maxFreq.

🟢 Algorithm
push(val)

Increase freq in freqMap.

Update maxFreq.

Add element to groupMap at that frequency.

pop()

Get stack at maxFreq.

Pop element.

Decrease frequency in freqMap.

If stack empty → reduce maxFreq.

Return element.

🟢 Java Code
import java.util.*;

class FreqStack {

    private Map<Integer, Integer> freqMap;
    private Map<Integer, Stack<Integer>> groupMap;
    private int maxFreq;

    public FreqStack() {
        freqMap = new HashMap<>();
        groupMap = new HashMap<>();
        maxFreq = 0;
    }

    public void push(int val) {

        int freq = freqMap.getOrDefault(val, 0) + 1;
        freqMap.put(val, freq);

        maxFreq = Math.max(maxFreq, freq);

        groupMap.putIfAbsent(freq, new Stack<>());
        groupMap.get(freq).push(val);
    }

    public int pop() {

        Stack<Integer> stack = groupMap.get(maxFreq);
        int val = stack.pop();

        freqMap.put(val, freqMap.get(val) - 1);

        if (stack.isEmpty()) {
            maxFreq--;
        }

        return val;
    }
}

🟢 Line-by-Line Explanation
🔹 freqMap
Map<Integer, Integer> freqMap;


Tracks frequency of each element.

🔹 groupMap
Map<Integer, Stack<Integer>> groupMap;


Groups elements by frequency.

Example:

groupMap = {
  1 : [5,7,4]
  2 : [5,7]
  3 : [5]
}

🔹 Update maxFreq
maxFreq = Math.max(maxFreq, freq);


Tracks highest frequency currently.

🔹 push(val)

Increase frequency and push element into stack of that freq.

🔹 pop()

Always remove from highest frequency stack.

